note: A line ending with a comma, "then" or "and" carries its sentence on to the next line.
let colors be a list of "red", "green",
    "blue" and
    "yellow".
say colors.
let ready be yes.
if ready then
    say "ready".
if ready,

    # a comment line in between is fine
    say "still ready".
let both be ready and
3 is 3.
say both.
to area with width and
        height:
    give back width times height.
say area of 2 and
    5.
say "done".
